  "notes": "USAGE:\n- {大敗|たいはい}を{喫|きっ}する (to suffer a crushing defeat)\n- {大敗|たいはい}する (to be heavily defeated)\n- {大敗|たいはい}を{味|あじ}わう (to taste a crushing defeat)\nCommonly used in sports, elections, and business contexts. Implies not just losing but losing badly.\n\nRELATED WORDS:\n- {惨敗|ざんぱい} (disastrous defeat - even stronger)\n- {完敗|かんぱい} (complete defeat)\n- {敗北|はいぼく} (defeat - general)\n- {大勝|たいしょう} (landslide victory - antonym)",
